meta {
  name: Upload Action Attachment
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/method/implementor.client_api.upload_action_attachment
  body: multipartForm
  auth: inherit
}

body:multipart-form {
  todo: 12glqu2bo8
  file: @file(/path/to/vat-certificate.pdf)
  ~note: VAT certificate, valid until 2027
  ~complete: 1
  ~project: PROJ-0029
  ~customer: Hamza
}

tests {
  test("returns 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("has message", function () {
    expect(res.body).to.have.property("message");
  });

  test("returns the open actions list", function () {
    expect(res.body.message).to.be.an("array");
  });
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Answers an action that asks for a file. One file per call.

  **Endpoint:** `POST /api/method/implementor.client_api.upload_action_attachment`  
  **Screen:** Waiting on you → Upload (actions with `cta` = `upload`)

  > ⚠️ **Changes data** on the shared server. Uploaded files can't be removed through the API. Use test records only.

  **Permission:** Signed-in client user (Client User or Client Admin). The action must be assigned to this user.

  **Body fields (multipart form):**

  | Field | Type | Required | Example | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `todo` | string | yes | `12glqu2bo8` | `name` from Waiting for you. |
  | `file` | file | yes* | `vat-certificate.pdf` | PDF, JPG or PNG. 10 MB max. |
  | `note` | string | no | `Valid until 2027` | Saved as a comment beside the file. |
  | `complete` | 0 or 1 | no | `1` | Send `1` with the **last** file to finish the action. |
  | `project` | string | no | `PROJ-0029` | Send it when Waiting on you was opened from a project: the reply then holds that project's open actions only. Must be the client's project. Disabled by default. |
  | `customer` | string | no | `Hamza` | Not used by the app. The server picks the user's company. Disabled by default. |

  \* Instead of a multipart `file`, you can send `filename` plus base64 `filedata` (the same way ticket attachments work).

  **Several files:** call once per file. Send `complete=1` only on the last call.

  **Response:** the updated list of **open** actions, same items as Waiting for you: for `project` when it is sent, else for all projects.

  ```json
  { "message": [ ... open actions ... ] }
  ```

  **What the server does:**

  - Attaches the file privately to the record the action is about (`reference`), or to the action itself if it has none.
  - Saves `note` (if given) as a comment on that same record.
  - With `complete=1`, marks the action done and notifies our team.

  **Repeating a call:**

  - On an action that is already done, the call uploads nothing and returns **200** with the current list, so a retry of the `complete=1` call is safe.
  - On an action that is still open (`complete` left out or `0`), every call stores the file again. A retry after a dropped connection creates a **duplicate** attachment (and note).

  **Errors:** client API errors have an `error_code`; auth errors raised by Frappe don't.

  - **401** (no error_code): token expired or invalid. Refresh once and retry, else sign out.
  - **403** (no error_code): no Authorization header sent.
  - **403** `not_permitted`: the action doesn't exist, or isn't assigned to this user; or `project` isn't this client's project.
  - **403** `no_client_linked`: the user isn't linked to any client company.
  - **417** `missing_parameter`: `todo` left out; or no multipart `file` and `filedata` or `filename` left out.
  - **417** `invalid_file_type`: not a PDF, JPG or PNG.
  - **417** `file_too_large`: over 10 MB.
  - **417** `invalid_file`: empty file or bad base64.
}
